1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E11 -= Standardized.Test =- Subripped by zerox

2
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:07,460
如入无人之境 这家伙真的势不可挡
And he's tearing up the board, folks. This man cannot be stopped.

3
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:09,680
凯罗，把看家本领拿出来吧 我准备好了，血气翻腾
All right, give me your best shot here, Carol. I feel hot. I feel ready.

4
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:11,540
好
Okay.

5
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:20,160
帕梅拉.邓肯纳德 理查德.加兰德主演的.
What 1957 Roger Corman film...

6
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:23,100
1957年罗杰.考曼的什么电影？
starred Pamela Duncan and Richard Garland?

7
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,140
你真的要问？
What, are they serious?

8
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:31,440
<巨蟹怪物>，来点难度好吗？
Attack of the Crab Monsters. Come on, give me a hard question, Carol.

9
00:01:33,047 --> 00:01:34,593
真不可思议
I don't believe it.

10
00:01:35,349 --> 00:01:37,157
凯罗，记得这歌吗？
Oh, wow, Carol, remember this song?

11
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:46,380
记得，我们小时候爸妈经常听
Yeah. Mom and Dad used to play this to us all the time when we we're little.

12
00:01:46,494 --> 00:01:48,097
记得我们以前会怎样吗？
Yeah, remember what we used to do?

13
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,180
这不是遗传的吧？
I hope this isn't hereditary.

14
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,880
同胞们，成绩单游戏
Hey, guys, report cards came.

15
00:02:46,053 --> 00:02:48,800
-成绩单游戏？ -这是你的
- Oh, yeah? Our report cards came? - Yeah. This is yours.

16
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:51,460
我们有个孩子喜欢成绩单
Maggie, we have a child who actually likes getting report cards.

17
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:53,040
我们到底做错了什么？
Where did we go wrong?

18
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,980
我知道成绩，但还是很紧张
I don't know why I'm so nervous. I mean, I already know what I got.

19
00:02:56,980 --> 00:03:00,580
对了，优，优，优，优..!
Yep. A, A, A, A, A, A!

20
00:03:01,402 --> 00:03:04,382
-太棒了，麦克 -太好了
- That's great, sweetie. Mike.... - Good for you.

21
00:03:07,908 --> 00:03:10,979
中，中，中，中.
C, C, C, C...

22
00:03:11,745 --> 00:03:13,917
差，良
D, B.

23
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:17,395
起码有一科良
Well, he did get one B.

24
00:03:18,686 --> 00:03:20,790
-体育？ -对了
- Phys Ed. ? - You got it.

25
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:24,940
-让我受不了的是.. -我知道，他很聪明
- What drives me crazy is that-- - I know, he's not dumb.

26
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:27,860
二年级时他都能得到良和优良
In first and second grade, he got Bs and B-pluses.

27
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:32,700
直到凯罗出现，全部拿优
Well, that was before Carol came along and started getting all As.

28
00:03:33,033 --> 00:03:35,171
-真有种 -是啊
- The nerve. - Yeah.

29
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:38,700
至少他风光了两年
Well, at least he had two great years.

30
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:42,840
比几百年前的人好多了
That's better than that poor guy a couple of popes ago.

31
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:44,760
杰森
Jason.

32
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,680
你也许要求太高了
Maggie, maybe we're being a little too hard on him, you know?

33
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,240
不是所有孩子都能拿优
Not all kids have to get As.

34
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:52,700
但是最近几年每况愈下
But for the last couple of years it's been getting worse.

35
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,520
这是青春期惹的祸
Well, that's what puberty's for.

36
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:58,180
碰到困难就认为穷途末路
You take a difficult situation and you make it impossible.

37
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:05,380
-麦克，去哪了？ -我去找杜克
- Where you been, Mike? - Oh, I thought I'd go look for Duke.

38
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:09,220
-麦克，杜克6个月前就走丢了 -啊？
- Mike, Duke ran away six months ago. - So?

39
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:10,640
而且不是我们的狗
And he wasn't our dog.

40
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:14,520
“我们的狗”是什么意思？
What does that really mean, Dad? "Our dog."

41
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:17,660
人有权利去拥有另一种生物吗？
I mean, can one person ever really own another living thing?

42
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:21,660
-我上楼去 -我看这样吧
- Maybe I should go look upstairs. - Hey, I got a great idea.

43
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,900
大家看看信对里面有什么
Why don't we all take a look at what's in this envelope?

44
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:25,960
好吧
Oh, okay.

45
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:31,280
“麦克.西弗，恭喜赢得2百万奖金”
"If your name is Mike Seaver, you may have already won $2 million."

46
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:36,120
妈妈，生气前请注意.
Hey, look, Mom, before you get too upset...

47
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,580
某些分数是有可能打错的
you should know that some of these grades might be wrong.

48
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:41,180
我们害怕的是有些打对了
What scares us is some of them might be right.

49
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:46,150
我得到中，并不差，中等
Hey, I got a C average. That's not bad, it's average.

50
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:50,460
你就是想得到中等？
Is that what you want to be, Mike? Average?

51
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:54,220
其实比中等高一点
Well, it's a high C, so actually it's a little above average.

52
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:58,680
-良好到中等之间？ -也没有那么高
- Don't they have C-pluses for that? - Well, it's not that high.

53
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:02,640
你可以拿更高分的
You can do better than this, can't you?

54
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,000
这不是我的错.
It's not my fault, Mom, I just....

55
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,900
我和老师有冲突
I have a personality conflict with my teacher.

56
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:09,400
麦克，6科6个不同的老师.
Mike, you have about the same grades...

57
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,940
你拿到的成绩都一样
in six different subjects with six different teachers.

58
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:13,160
我知道
I know.

59
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:16,840
我不喜欢的人都喜欢去当老师
The profession just seems to attract people who are difficult to get along with.

60
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,780
我们还要说多少遍？
Mike, how many times do we have to go through this?

61
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:22,680
你需要努力一点
I mean, you're just going to have to work a little harder.

62
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:24,620
我很努力了
I am working hard.

63
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,840
为什么我每次上楼.
Then why is it every time I go up to your room...

64
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,220
你应该在房间里学习时.
when you're supposed to be studying...

65
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:30,920
我却看到你睡觉，掷飞镖
you're either napping or throwing darts?

66
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,580
我需要轻松一下
That's how I unwind.

67
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:34,520
麦克.
Mike.

68
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:38,900
你已经尽力了？
Look, Mike, are you saying that you're trying as hard as you can?

69
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:40,320
是的
Yeah.

70
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:43,400
这些“中等”就是你的最高水平？
So these Cs are honestly the best you can do?

71
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,500
我可以超过“中等”的
No, I can get better than Cs, Dad.

72
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:49,000
几何这科怎么得差了？
Well, Mike, what about this D in geometry?

73
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:51,400
不知道
I don't know.

74
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:54,960
课程太难了？
Are the classes too hard for you?

75
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:59,900
你需要选容易一点的数学课吗？
I mean, would you rather be in a math section that's a little less demanding?

76
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,220
爸爸，我有能力的 我不是及格了吗？
Dad, I can do it. Look, I'm passing, aren't l?

77
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:05,040
别让我跟傻瓜一起上课
Like, you don't have to go putting me in with the rejects.

78
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,140
凯克，还玩吗？
Hey, Mike, want to finish our game?

79
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,360
不打扰你欣赏“优秀”成绩单了
No, I wouldn't want to keep you from admiring your As.

80
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,840
-继续吧，不妨碍你 -拜托
- Please, go ahead. Don't let me stop you. - Come on, Mike.

81
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:22,480
别谦虚，一起分享这个时刻
Oh, don't be modest, Carol. Come on, let's share this special moment.

82
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:25,860
凯罗，真让人骄傲
Oh, I'm so proud of you, Carol.

83
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:29,920
代数：优! 社会科：优!
Algebra : A! Social Studies: A!

84
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:34,140
-书呆子科：特优! -我不是书呆子
- Advanced Nerdiness: A+! - I'm not a nerd.

85
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,900
书呆子也没什么不好
Hey, Carol, there's nothing wrong with being a nerd.

86
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:40,820
没有书呆子 还有谁去买学校的东西？
I mean, without nerds, who would buy all the back-to-school supplies?

87
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:44,020
还有谁去约会数学队的人？
Who would date the guys on the math team?

88
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:48,300
还有谁上课时举手？
And who would raise their hand in class and go, "Ooh, ooh"?

89
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:53,040
你得不到好成绩，所以妒忌我
Well, you're just jealous because you never get good grades.

90
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,680
若是我肯学习，我会拿优的
Look, if I studied, I could probably get all As.

91
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:59,660
若是有吃饭课，你也拿不到优秀
You couldn't get an A in Lunch as a Second Language.

92
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,360
真有意思，凯罗 有考虑过当相声演员吗？
Oh, that's funny, Carol. Have you ever considered being a standup?

93
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:05,560
可以谈化学喜剧
Maybe you could do, like, chemistry comedy and stuff.

94
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:06,960
你真是个混蛋
You are such a jerk.

95
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:10,260
可以拿好成绩，干嘛不去学习？
I mean, if you could get such good grades, then why don't you study?

96
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:12,680
因为我还有更重要的事
Because I have better things to do.

97
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:16,080
例如呢？ 让罗依德的鼻孔喷牛奶？
Like what? Like getting Lloyd Kreeger to laugh milk out of his nose?

98
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:21,560
不，例如跟朋友一起玩 某些人连朋友都没有
No. Like hanging out with friends, which certain people don't have.

99
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:22,740
好吧.
Yeah, well....

100
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:25,220
周一看看谁更聪明？
We'll just see how smart you are on Monday, won't we?

101
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:27,580
周一怎么了？
Why, what's Monday?

102
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:32,280
全校参加爱达荷智力测试
It's the day the whole school takes the Idaho Standardized Test.

103
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:35,680
我若是温习一下 或许拿全校最高分
So? If I study, I'll probably get the highest grade in school.

104
00:07:35,876 --> 00:07:38,840
笨蛋，这种测试是无法温习的
You can't study for this test, bonebrain.

105
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:41,120
这是智力测试
It's an aptitude test.

106
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:42,720
我知道
I know.

107
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,920
什么是智力测试？
What's an aptitude test?

108
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:51,480
就是IQ测试，看看人有多聪明
It's basically an IQ test. To see how smart you are.

109
00:07:51,558 --> 00:07:54,299
在你的角度，是测试你有多愚蠢
Or, in your case, how smart you aren't.

110
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:07,220
听好了，这是爱达荷智力测试
All right, now, listen up. This is the Idaho Standardized Test.

111
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:11,120
我讨厌测验，讨厌这种铅笔
God, I hate these tests. I hate number two pencils.

112
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:13,800
讨厌这种经历
I hate this whole experience.

113
00:08:14,715 --> 00:08:17,490
冷静点，没什么大不了
Hey, look, calm down, will you? This isn't such a big deal.

114
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:19,580
没什么大不了？
Not a big.... Not a big deal?

115
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:22,880
我大腿上的豆豆都冒汗了
Tell that to the hives that are breaking out on my thighs.

116
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:26,360
你大腿上长豆豆了？
You get hives on your thighs?

117
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:27,700
-要看看吗？ -不了，我相信你
- You want to see them? - No, I believe you.

118
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,100
天哪
Oh, my God.

119
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:36,220
这些测试不算进成绩单
This test doesn't even count on your grades.

120
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,940
测验结果有何关系？
I mean, what difference does it make what you get?

121
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:41,140
开玩笑，这是IQ测试
Are you kidding? This is an IQ test.

122
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:44,240
比成绩重要10倍
This is 10 times more important than your grades.

123
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,800
等等，你在说什么？
Wait. What are you talking about?

124
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:51,060
这测试能判断我们有多聪明
This test decides once and for all how smart we are.

125
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:54,600
从今尔后 父母就会知道我们多笨
I mean, after today, our parents will know how stupid we are.

126
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:58,440
兄弟姐妹就会知道我们多笨
Our brothers and sisters will know how stupid we are.

127
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:04,000
也许整个爱达荷州 也会知道我们有多笨
I can only assume the whole state of Idaho will know how stupid we are.

128
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:07,160
父母也会知道成绩？
Our parents get these results?

129
00:09:08,435 --> 00:09:10,778
说起来就长了
I'll never hear the end of it.

130
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:15,600
“可怜的里奇，没有他哥哥戴维聪明”
"Poor Richie, he's just not as smart as his brother David.

131
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:18,980
“戴维今年要到普林斯顿大学念法学”
"Our David is pre-law at Princeton this year.

132
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:22,820
“里奇，倒垃圾去”
"Oh, hi, Richie, could you take out the garbage, please?

133
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:27,320
“也许以后这就是他的行业”
"We're hoping he can do it professionally someday."

134
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:31,200
你哥哥又怎样了？
Look, what do you care about your brother?

135
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:33,220
只是个书呆子 谁家里没有书呆子？
I mean, so he's a nerd. Every family's got a nerd.

136
00:09:34,394 --> 00:09:36,941
对了，你也有凯罗
Hey, yeah, that's right. You got Carol.

137
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:38,480
她是个天才
She's a genius.

138
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:41,520
你站在她旁边就像一头猪
You're gonna look like a tree stump next to her.

139
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:46,240
才不是
No, I'm not.

140
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:46,340
其一，我和她是一样聪明的
Because for one thing, I am just as smart as she is.

141
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:46,440
其二，我不相信这种测试
And for another thing, I happen not to believe in these tests.

142
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:46,540
瞧我干什么？我连题目都不看
I mean, you know what I do? I don't even read the questions.

143
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:46,640
我在答卡上画图，这样
I just fill in these computer dots in a pretty pattern, like this.

144
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:46,740
考试开始
All right. You may begin.

145
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:46,840
你疯了，干什么？
What? You're crazy. What are you doing?

146
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:46,940
这是自画像 爱达荷州的人也喜欢这个
Oh, it's a self-portrait. They'll love this in Idaho.

147
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:47,040
埃维斯先生
All right, Mr. Ellis...

148
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:47,140
今天结束前还有什么要说吗？
is there anything else you'd like to talk about before we stop for today?

149
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:47,240
-没有了，一切都很好 -好
- Nope. Everything's just great. - Good.

150
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:47,340
你的问题大大改善了
Okay. Well, I think we're making some real progress here with your problem.

151
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:47,440
我有什么问题？
What problem's that?

152
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:47,540
你有习来惯性撒谎的问题
Well, Mr. Ellis, we both know, don't we, that you're an habitual liar?

153
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:47,640
没有
No, I'm not.

154
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,580
-埃维斯先生.. -好吧
- Mr. Ellis.... - Okay, okay.

155
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:52,720
别逼问我
Don't pressure me like this.

156
00:10:54,341 --> 00:10:56,411
我的人生要完了
My whole life is going down the drain.

157
00:10:57,060 --> 00:11:01,100
一分钟前你还说“一切很好”
But, now, just a minute ago, you said, "Everything is just great."

158
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,080
没有
No, I didn't.

159
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:06,760
这.
Well, then...

160
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:11,500
我们下次要好好聊聊
we certainly do have a lot to talk about next time, Mr. Ellis.

161
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:15,140
下次？我再也不回来
What next time? I'm never coming back here again.

162
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:18,100
-随便你 -好吧
- Whatever you say. - Fine.

163
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:21,520
-下周一见 -好的
- See you next Wednesday? - Good. Yeah.

164
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:27,360
本，来吧
All right, Ben. et's do it.

165
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:30,560
-爸爸 -本
- Dad.... - Come on, Ben.

166
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:34,060
我没有要求你做过什么 希望你不要推搪
I don't ask you to do too much around here. When I do, I expect it to get done.

167
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:35,700
-爸爸，但是.. -不得异议
- But, Dad-- - Without an argument.

168
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,380
晚点行不行？
Can't I do it later?

169
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:40,060
-本，别惹我 -好吧
- Ben, you're testing me, now. - All right.

170
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:42,340
这才像样
That's more like it.

171
00:11:58,620 --> 00:12:05,340
-本，真是颗天生的星星 -什么意思？
- Ben, you're a born Pip. - What's a Pip?

172
00:12:05,746 --> 00:12:07,417
一种精神境界
A state of mind.

173
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:11,940
喂？
Hello?

174
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:15,440
等等，找你的
Okay, wait one second. It's for you.

175
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:20,180
别走，还没完
Don't go away, now. We're not done.

176
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:21,940
喂
Hello.

177
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:28,709
我老婆不在家
Well, no, my wife is at work.

178
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:33,460
对，当然了，既然那么重要
Yes.... Yes, of course, if it's important.

179
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,020
好吧，到时候见
All right, I'll see you then.

180
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,260
本，关掉音乐
Hey, Ben, will you turn that off, please?

181
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:45,920
喂，麦姬
Yeah, Maggie?

182
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:48,620
半小时后能赶到学校吗？
Can you meet me down at the high school in about a half an hour?

183
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:52,680
学校的心理医师，关于麦克
Well, it's the school psychologist. It's about Mike.

184
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:57,964
西弗先生太太，我们非常关心.
Dr. and Mrs. Seaver, we have some concern over....

185
00:12:57,964 --> 00:12:59,408
薄荷糖？不要？
Breath mint? No.

186
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:03,340
-..麦克的IQ测试 -什么成绩？
- Over the results of Mikes IQ test. - Why? What did he get?

187
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:06,060
麦姬，这种测试很主观
Now, Maggie, you know, these are highly subjective.

188
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:09,680
许多医师甚至不考虑.
Many diagnosticians, they don't even consider these to mean....

189
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:11,840
-他的成绩多少？ -他的分数是.
- What did he get? - He got....

190
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:14,480
我先告诉你分数的含义
Well, let me just put this in context for you, Mrs. Seaver.

191
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:20,280
100分是中等，120是非常聪明.
Now, a score of 100 is about average, 120 is very bright...

192
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:24,040
140是天才，160是.
140 is considered a genius, 160 is--

193
00:13:24,157 --> 00:13:26,431
-麦克得到多少？ -27分
- What did Mike get? - A 27.

194
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:31,760
什么？荒谬，明显搞错了
What? This is ridiculous. I mean, this is obviously a mistake.

195
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:34,780
对不起，西弗太太 我们已经反复校对
I'm sorry, Mrs. Seaver. We've checked and double-checked.

196
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,360
-木糖醇？ -不要了
- Antacid? - No.

197
00:13:37,337 --> 00:13:38,849
27分？
Twenty-seven?

198
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:40,940
你是心理医生那就好了
I'm glad that you're a psychiatrist, Dr. Seaver.

199
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:42,820
你明白我的意思吗？
You'll understand what I'm saying here.

200
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,880
你说我的儿子是傻瓜
Yeah, you're saying my son is an idiot.

201
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,360
不，严格来说是低能
No, technically, he's an imbecile.

202
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:49,920
什么？
What?

203
00:13:50,517 --> 00:13:54,123
1至25是傻瓜，25至50是低能
Well, 0 to 25 is an idiot. 25 to 50 is an imbecile.

204
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:56,360
那我们就放心了
Well, that's certainly a load off my mind.

205
00:13:57,124 --> 00:14:00,969
60到70是白痴
et's see, I believe that 60 to 70 is a moron.

206
00:14:00,994 --> 00:14:04,099
50到60是什么？
No, wait. What's 50 to 60?

207
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,380
不知道，头大无脑？
I don't know. A bozo?

208
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:07,520
不
No!

209
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,400
算了，这个跟麦克没有关系
Never mind. This has nothing to do with Mike.

210
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:12,720
对，根据测试结果.
No. Because according to this...

211
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:15,240
麦克距离头大无脑还很遥远呢
Mike could never even aspire to become a bozo.

212
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:19,760
西弗先生太太，我们不能反应过度
Now, Dr. and Mrs. Seaver, the worst thing we can do is to overreact to this.

213
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:22,880
麦克最近有撞到头部吗？
Has Mike taken a sharp blow to the head recently?

214
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:24,300
没有
No.

215
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:27,700
有过长的缺氧吗？
Suffered any prolonged oxygen deprivation?

216
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:31,180
我儿子没有大脑损伤
No, Dr. Marlens, our son is not brain-damaged.

217
00:14:31,420 --> 00:14:32,740
好吧，只是确保万一
Okay. Just checking.

218
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:35,780
麦克的档案说明.
Now look, Mike's file indicates he's always had a....

219
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:38,360
他有叛逆性
Well, how shall we say, a problem with authority.

220
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:42,320
例如这里写的去年.
For example, it says here that last year...

221
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:45,660
他把小老鼠.
he placed a litter of baby gerbils...

222
00:14:46,306 --> 00:14:49,320
放到布赖来恩老师的面巾盒里
into Mrs. O'Brien's Kleenex box...

223
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:51,060
接着她用面巾擦鼻子
and when she went to blow her nose....

224
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,840
那老家伙真的.
That old bag must have just....

225
00:14:56,260 --> 00:14:57,240
不好意思
Excuse me.

226
00:14:57,760 --> 00:15:01,480
我只是寓工作于娱乐 这里还有很多好东西
There's so little joy in my job, and he's got a lot of good stuff in here.

227
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:03,600
谢谢
Thank you.

228
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:06,920
你的意思是？
Dr. Marlens, what are you getting at?

229
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:08,460
瞧这个
You see this?

230
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:12,280
这是正常的答卡，很凌乱
This is a normal test answer sheet. It's a mess.

231
00:15:12,465 --> 00:15:16,173
答案随机分布在页面上，瞧这个
The little dots are scattered randomly around the page. You see this?

232
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,260
你儿子的答卡
This is your son's test answer sheet.

233
00:15:18,680 --> 00:15:21,580
在画面上构成图形，有房子，飞机.
The dots make up little pictures of houses, airplanes.

234
00:15:21,660 --> 00:15:24,680
瞧这里，是个女性的身体
Look here, there's even one of a young woman's body in profile.

235
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,180
好身材
Nice figure.

236
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:31,040
你是说麦克是故意的
So, you're saying.... You're saying that Mike did this intentionally.

237
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:34,980
要不然麦克就是个 有艺术才华的低能儿
Well, either that, Mrs. Seaver, or he's a highly artistic imbecile.

238
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:54,260
弹什么？很好听
What is it? That's pretty.

239
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:55,320
没什么
Nothing.

240
00:15:57,980 --> 00:16:01,420
听说今天你见家长了
Well, I heard you got called down to the school psychologist today.

241
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:04,060
是的，爸妈现在学校
Oh, yeah. Mom and Dad are down there right now.

242
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,560
是吗？你做些什么了？
They are? Why? What'd you do?

243
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:10,093
我IQ测试拿了27分
Well, I got a 27 on my IQ test.

244
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:15,560
爸妈不会在乎这种测试的.
Mom and Dad really don't care about that sort of thing, so, you know...

245
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:16,540
别难过.
don't feel bad.

246
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:19,540
你拿到27分？
You got a 27?

247
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:23,740
笨蛋，我是故意的
Yeah, I did it on purpose, bonehead.

248
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,720
-我甚至没有看题目 -什么？
- I mean, I didn't even read the questions. - What?

249
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:30,644
我知道自己聪明 为什么浪费宝贵的时间.
I mean, I know I'm brilliant, so I figured, why waste my valuable time...

250
00:16:30,644 --> 00:16:32,054
去玩填字游戏？
on playing fill-in-the-dots?

251
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,940
不是吧
Come on, you didn't really do that.

252
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,340
凯罗，怎么说呢
Carol, how should I put this?

253
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:42,760
在你出生前，爸妈曾对我说.
You see before you we're born, Mom and Dad came to me and they said:

254
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:46,780
“麦克，我们希望下一个孩子能读书”
"Mike, we hope that our next child isn't some goody-goody nerdface...

255
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:51,760
“要像你一样，能独立思考”
"but that he's a real independent, free-thinker, like you."

256
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:53,160
是的
Yeah.

257
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:56,180
他们不知道你的智力达到了峰值
Little did they know, you had peaked intellectually.

258
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,200
麦克.
Mike?

259
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:01,860
他们会打死你的
They're gonna kill you.

260
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:06,140
也许他们发现这种测试的无聊后.
Carol, maybe Mom and Dad have realized how stupid these tests are.

261
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:08,880
他们会敬仰我的做法
Maybe they're gonna admire me for what I did.

262
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,940
麦克，可以说两句吗？
Mike. Could we speak to you for a moment, please?

263
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:19,520
他们要正式地打死你
Maybe they're gonna have you killed professionally.

264
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:29,720
麦克，请解释这是什么？
Mike, can you explain to us what this is?

265
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,340
好吧
Oh, okay.

266
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:36,120
这是波音747，这是大鲈鱼.
This here is a Boeing 747, and this is a largemouth bass...

267
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,860
这是罗来恩达的肖像
and this.... This is a full-body profile of Rhonda Tishkin.

268
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:44,060
麦克，为什么这样做？
Mike, why did you do this?

269
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:45,800
她身材很好
She's got a great body, Mom.

270
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:49,640
这可不是说笑，为什么这样做？
Mike, this isn't a joke. Come on, why did you do that?

271
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,900
不知道，我就喜欢这样
I don't know. I just felt like it.

272
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,680
喜欢这样？
You just felt like it.

273
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:58,160
我不知道你们如此在乎这些测试
Well, gee, I didn't realize how important these tests we're to you guys.

274
00:17:58,520 --> 00:18:00,240
你们应该早告诉我.
Maybe you should have told me that you we're only interested...

275
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:01,980
我们只在乎高IQ的孩子
in having kids with high IQ scores.

276
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:04,060
麦克
Mike.

277
00:18:08,220 --> 00:18:08,700
麦克
Mike.

278
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:11,520
没关系 你们已经有一个聪明的孩子
Hey, that's okay. I mean, you guys got one smart kid.

279
00:18:11,578 --> 00:18:14,285
“优秀”女士也许能成为宇航员.
Miss Straight As here can go and become an astronaut...

280
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:16,540
麦克打杂就好了，没关系
and Mikey can always mix the Tang, no problem.

281
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:22,280
让他冷静一下吧
Why don't we just let him cool off?

282
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:24,500
-好吧？ -好吧
- Okay. - Okay?

283
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,420
干什么？
What do you want?

284
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:44,380
没什么，我.
Nothing, really, I mean, I just--

285
00:18:44,644 --> 00:18:46,122
走开
Then why don't you just get out of here?

286
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:51,140
麦克，你并不笨
Look, Mike. You're not really stupid.

287
00:18:51,684 --> 00:18:55,699
谢谢你，凯罗 我感到你的光芒了
Well, thanks, Carol. I am deeply touched by your superiority.

288
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,840
麦克，别感到愚蠢
I hope I don't make you feel stupid, Mike.

289
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:01,140
那你走开就好了
You don't make me feel stupid. Just get out of here, okay?

290
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:03,880
没有人感到愚蠢，因为我不愚蠢
Nobody makes me feel stupid, "cause I'm not stupid.

291
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:06,440
我不是这样说了吗？
I just said that.

292
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,960
也许我因为愚蠢，听不懂
Well, maybe I was just too stupid to understand.

293
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:12,280
麦克，拜托.
Mike, come on. I mean...

294
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:15,440
你老是说我是书呆子.
you're always calling me a nerd and stuff...

295
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:19,620
我当时只是想报复你
and I don't know, I guess I was just trying to get you back.

296
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:24,840
因为你更成熟，更酷
I guess "cause you're older, and cooler and everything.

297
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:29,840
我就觉得.
And I just figured that...

298
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:32,460
只有我一个人难过
I was the only one who was getting hurt.

299
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:36,000
我是个书呆子.
I mean, I am sort of a nerd...

300
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:38,760
但你不蠢
but you're not really stupid.

301
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:44,780
你得“优秀”，我得“中等” 这是巧合吗？
Oh, so, I guess it's just coincidence that you get all the As and I get all the Cs?

302
00:19:45,060 --> 00:19:47,980
我也不知道为什么你成绩不好
Look, I don't know why you don't get good grades. I mean....

303
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:51,880
或许是因为.
Well, maybe it has something to do with the fact...

304
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:54,040
你在做功课时睡觉，掷飞镖
that you sleep and play darts while doing your homework.

305
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:56,140
飞镖有什么不好？
What is it with the darts?

306
00:19:56,449 --> 00:19:59,588
这里没有人懂得放松了吗？
I mean, am I the only guy around here that knows how to unwind?

307
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:02,180
听好了.
Okay, listen.

308
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:06,660
麦克斯.怀来恩伯格什么时候.. 替布鲁斯.斯普林斯丁打鼓伴奏？
What year did Max Weinberg start playing drums for Bruce Springsteen?

309
00:20:07,393 --> 00:20:09,565
怎么撇开话题了？
Hey, did we just start a new conversation?

310
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:10,940
说吧，什么时候？
Come on, what year?

311
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:13,740
1973年，什么意思？
1973. So what does that mean?

312
00:20:14,740 --> 00:20:18,620
意思是麦克斯.怀来恩伯格的收入 会激增.
Well, aside from being a huge boost in income for Max Weinberg...

313
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:21,780
还有你很聪明
it means you're pretty smart.

314
00:20:22,740 --> 00:20:25,020
因为记住了这种没用的事情？
What, cause I know one useless fact?

315
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:27,840
你记住了数不清的没用的事情
You know millions of useless facts.

316
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:31,800
例如什么<巨蟹怪兽>
I mean, like the Attack of the Crab People thing.

317
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:34,900
-真的难以相信 -是<巨蟹怪物>
- I mean, I couldn't believe that. - Crab Monsters, Carol.

318
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,540
<巨蟹怪物的袭击>
Attack of the Crab Monsters.

319
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:40,680
你记不住考试的内容
See, I mean, you don't remember things for tests.

320
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:43,880
因为某种原因.
You just remember things you want to remember...

321
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:47,520
你只记住想记住的事情
for some strange reason.

322
00:20:48,334 --> 00:20:50,060
记性好算什么
So I have a good memory. Big deal.

323
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:53,000
还不止呢.
It's more than just that. I mean.... Okay.

324
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:56,500
记得情人节你借了我20块吗？
Remember last year when you borrowed $20 from me on Valentines Day?

325
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,280
是的
Yeah. So?

326
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:02,540
-我让你写借据 -我乐意写
- And I made you sign an IOU? - Which I gladly did.

327
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:08,680
你说2月29日还我
Promising to pay me back on February 29th.

328
00:21:08,922 --> 00:21:11,595
到了1988年我会还你
Hey, come 1988, that $20 is yours.

329
00:21:12,825 --> 00:21:16,670
那做法不但很聪明.
You see, that, that wasn't just intelligent...

330
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:18,940
而且很有创造性
that was actually very creative.

331
00:21:23,403 --> 00:21:25,177
不，是你笨而已
No, you we're just a sucker.

332
00:21:25,360 --> 00:21:27,860
这就是我的意思
You see, that's my point. I mean...

333
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:30,240
我经常做傻事
I do dumb things all the time.

334
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:34,680
你喜欢时就会做聪明的事
And you do smart things when you feel like it.

335
00:21:35,248 --> 00:21:37,295
-这.. -但是.
- Well.... - But, hey.

336
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:40,760
妈妈不是经常骂你别自作聪明吗？
Why do you think Moms always telling you to shut your smart mouth?

337
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:44,580
要做到这般讨厌 还是需要一定的智力和努力的
I mean, it takes brains and hard work to be as obnoxious as you are.

338
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:49,640
是的
Yeah, I guess it does.

339
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:53,780
喜欢做的事情谈不上努力
But when you love what you do, it really doesn't seem like work.

340
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:58,179
去他的，也许我们的IQ一样呢
I mean, heck, for all we know, you and I might have the same IQ.

341
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,240
是啊，也许我比你高呢
Yeah, who knows? Mine might even be higher.

342
00:22:00,273 --> 00:22:02,286
别歇斯底里了
et's not get hysterical, now.

343
00:22:03,320 --> 00:22:05,260
-凯罗 -嗯？
- Hey, Carol? - Yeah?

344
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:05,700
谢谢
Thanks.

345
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:11,800
-你这混蛋 -书呆子
- You jerk. - Nerd.

346
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:13,700
我是善意的
I meant that in a nice way.

347
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:37,700
谢谢你，非常感谢
Oh, good, thank you. Yes, thank you very much.

348
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:38,320
好吧，再见
All right. Bye-bye.

349
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:42,482
老师说你可以再来一次 爱达荷智力测试
Hey, Mike, Dr. Marlens says you can take that Idaho Test over again...

350
00:22:42,482 --> 00:22:44,358
周六早上10点
Saturday morning, 10:00.

351
00:22:44,651 --> 00:22:46,254
爸爸，太好了 只不过.
Oh, that's great, Dad, but....

352
00:22:46,280 --> 00:22:48,700
我很满意27分这个分数
Well, I've been thinking about it and I'm kind of happy with the 27.

353
00:22:49,722 --> 00:22:52,702
-麦克 -好吧，10点
- Mike. - Yes, Dad. Okay, 10:00.

